# Recheck Implementation Checklist

Run after every implementation task — no exceptions.

---

## Step 1 — Code Quality

- [ ] Remove all redundant, dead, and commented-out code
- [ ] No `console.log` or debug statements left
- [ ] No `any` TypeScript types — strict types throughout
- [ ] No duplicate Tailwind classes or inline styles
- [ ] Barrel exports (`index.ts`) updated if new files added

## Step 2 — Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Verify each acceptance criterion is implemented
- [ ] Verify against Figma design (if provided) — call Figma MCP `get_design_context` to confirm

## Step 3 — Build Validation

- [ ] Run AOT build: `ng build`
- [ ] Zero build errors, zero warnings (treat warnings as errors)
- [ ] Check `dist/` output size — flag if unexpectedly large

## Step 4 — Browser Validation

- [ ] Open in browser and visually verify
- [ ] Test dark mode and light mode toggle
- [ ] Test responsive breakpoints (mobile, tablet, desktop)
- [ ] If Three.js component: verify animation runs, no console WebGL errors

## Step 5 — Three.js Specific (if applicable)

- [ ] `cancelAnimationFrame` called on component destroy
- [ ] `renderer.dispose()` called on destroy
- [ ] `geometry.dispose()` called on destroy
- [ ] `material.dispose()` called on destroy
- [ ] `scene.clear()` called on destroy
- [ ] No WebGL context leaks (verify in DevTools: no "WebGL context lost" warning)
- [ ] `setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2))` present
- [ ] SSR guard: Three.js init inside `afterNextRender()` + `isPlatformBrowser()`
- [ ] Resize handler updates camera aspect, renderer size, and pixel ratio uniform

## Step 6 — Performance

- [ ] All components use `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`
- [ ] No Observables without `takeUntilDestroyed()` or `DestroyRef` cleanup
- [ ] Signals used for local state (not BehaviorSubject)
- [ ] Lighthouse performance score ≥ 85 (check before release)

## Step 7 — Security

- [ ] No `innerHTML` with unsanitized data
- [ ] No `bypassSecurityTrust*` without documented reason
- [ ] Three.js shaders: GLSL is static string only
- [ ] SSR: `inject(PLATFORM_ID)` used, no direct `window`/`document` access

## Step 8 — Tests

- [ ] Run: `ng test`
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Run: `ng test --coverage`
- [ ] Coverage ≥ 70%
- [ ] Three.js component: cleanup test and theme reactivity test present

## Step 9 — Documentation

- [ ] Update `ARCHITECTURE.md` if structure changed
- [ ] JSDoc on public service methods
- [ ] Remove comment-narration (no "// increment counter" style comments)

---

Repeat until all checks pass. No task is complete without this checklist.
